  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.6186 accuracy, showing that multiprofile with avgpool aggregation provides a large jump over singleprofile (~9% gain). The key remaining uncertainty within this best-performing direction is whether the aggregation method itself can be improved: avgpool treats all profiles symmetrically and independently, whereas a transformer aggregator can learn data-dependent attention weights across profiles, potentially capturing inter-profile interactions that averaging discards. config_020 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer (keeping concat fusion, resnet50, pca_n2000, multiprofile identical to config_018), cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. This is the best use of experiment 5 because it is a one-variable extension of the current best result, directly tests whether a more expressive aggregation mechanism can push accuracy further, and the answer will inform whether to invest remaining budget in transformer-based aggregation or in other axes (stronger image encoder, learned RNA encoders) with the 5 remaining experiments."
}

